# Design

This page should be a stunning yet short landingage for the marketing campaign. The brand should be undoubtly CDTM with high-finish, eye-catching, and storytelling touches. Details in `docs/brand.md`.

## Tokens (non-negotiable)

- Headlines: **Montserrat** (`font-heading`, 700 / `font-bold`). Body and UI: **Inter** (`font-sans`, 400 / 600).
- Weights **400 / 600 / 700** (`font-normal` / `font-semibold` / `font-bold`). No `font-extrabold` or `font-black`.
- Palette: main blue `#004EA8` (`cdtm-brand`), light blue `#91BEFF` (`cdtm-blue-light`), neutral `#E1F5FE` (`cdtm-neutral`), main green `#0F4C2D` (`cdtm-green`), light green `#5BA55A` (`cdtm-green-light`). Black / white as-is. Muted `#A1A1AA` (`cdtm-zinc-mid`) for secondary type on black.
- Light green is an **accent**, never body text. Neutral for cool light surfaces. Primary actions: main blue, not green-on-white.
- Paper grain: `src/assets/texture.jpg` + `.cdtm-texture` on a token fill (hero). CTA: `.cta-wash` (brand / light blue / neutral atmosphere), no grain. Don't invent a second noise recipe.

## Quality

- Type-led. Generous space. One `h1`. Display sizes should feel campaign-scale on desktop and readable on a phone.
- Effects (scroll, letter play, hover) should earn their keep. One strong idea in the hero beats decoration in every section.
- High-finish and details matter. This should be no standard page, the quality of the program needs to be visible on the site as well.
- Storytelling is key. The design is not only responsible for making the page look "good", it should strongly assist in telling the story of the campaign.
- Contrast on text and buttons. Primary actions: brand blue, not light-green-on-white.
- Every layout works from ~375px to desktop. Touch targets ~44px. Don't hide a whole section behind hover.
- Light page. No theme toggle.

## Logos and media

Use the provided CDTM and LMU SVGs. Don't recreate the wordmark in CSS. Alumni images only when provided, real `alt` text, no generated fake portraits.

## Freedom

Unusual story layout and stronger motion are in scope if they stay on-token and on-message.
